        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Those appear to be **Amazon purchases**, but the bank statement only shows the merchant descriptors, not the exact items:\n\n- **AMAZON MARK* HX5A631I3 SEATTLE WA**\n  - \"AMAZON MARK*\" usually indicates an Amazon Marketplace purchase from a third-party seller on Amazon.\n\n- **AMAZON RETA* PE3U01VX3 SEATTLE WA**\n  - \"AMAZON RETA*\" often refers to a retail purchase through Amazon (sometimes a regular Amazon order, digital item, or other Amazon transaction).\n\nTo find exactly what they were:\n\n1. Log in to your Amazon account.\n2. Go to **Your Orders**.\n3. Check orders placed around **May 30, 2026**.\n4. Match the order totals to the amounts on your bank statement.\n\nIf you don't recognize them:\n- Check **Archived Orders**.\n- Check other household members' Amazon accounts.\n- Look under **Memberships & Subscriptions**.\n- Review **Amazon Pay** transactions.\n\nIf you share the **amounts** of the charges (you can crop out any sensitive information), I can help narrow down what type of Amazon transactions they likely were."
          ]
        },
